                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "бати́стах"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "768f2322-0a3b-4180-8195-ccf66af4ecd4",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "бати́сту"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "65245a28-2033-3eee-b7da-79f9e2828940",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "текст. тонкая, полупрозрачная льняная или хлопчатобумажная ткань, вырабатываемая из крученой пряжи"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4236ffe9-0399-4b66-a482-a52bce35a1c0",
                                "sense_id": "65245a28-2033-3eee-b7da-79f9e2828940",
                                "text": "На этом торгу продаются только одни остатки, начиная от дорогого бархата до самых дешёвых тафтяных лент, от воздушных газов и индийской кисеи до толстого миткаля и тридцатикопеечных ситцев, от мягкого, шелковистого терно до грубого фриза и от белоснежного батиста до простой посконной холстины."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d63bec5d-7e85-3036-a9cf-f9066d98668d",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "текст. изделия из такой ткани"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee0e2278-1857-487a-8f30-a62527f2d45c",
                                "sense_id": "d63bec5d-7e85-3036-a9cf-f9066d98668d",
                                "text": "Лиза под окном в зале шила себе серенькое платье из сурового батиста; было утро знойного дня; со стола только что убрали завтрак, и в зале было совершенно тихо."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2625beb-1d0a-3aa5-9b6e-2f41b5088dac",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. предмет роскоши, дорогой ткани, богатства"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bda8aef-29a4-4c65-ba6a-d82ae1917312",
                                "sense_id": "b2625beb-1d0a-3aa5-9b6e-2f41b5088dac",
                                "text": "Ему всякий день завивали волосы пуклями, которые спускались до плеч, водили его в шелку, в батисте, в бархате, в перьях и в соболях по Невскому проспекту."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54d278c5-045a-487a-afa3-d808a4fe2adb",
                                "sense_id": "b2625beb-1d0a-3aa5-9b6e-2f41b5088dac",
                                "text": "Он с рождения, я думаю, упал в батист и кружева."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f9d066b-32e3-32ab-b3ad-3fffbf4a0442",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., поэт. то, что нежностью или цветом напоминает такую ткань"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "339a07fb-253e-4f0e-868c-5d8f6a3ce691",
                                "sense_id": "1f9d066b-32e3-32ab-b3ad-3fffbf4a0442",
                                "text": "Но белей и свежей кисеи и батиста миловидное личико Дуни, самокатного жемчуга краше перловые зубы, камней самоцветных светлее синие очи…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26da7f96-ba7b-3fd8-872f-43ce1fd234de",
                        "entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. батистовый платок"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc6f72bc-4004-4bd7-8b58-0f633012575e",
                                "sense_id": "26da7f96-ba7b-3fd8-872f-43ce1fd234de",
                                "text": "Бригадный генерал слезы батистом утирает, полковой командир ручкой отмахивается, батальонный уж и смеху лишился ― только хрюкает."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c9325a6-4615-42ce-be17-a69f64c039a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "target_lang_word": "cambric",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cambric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23bff8ad-3dee-38ca-afa3-99626b856140",
                                        "entry_id": "bd8e89b0-781d-3d1a-972d-7b0032395b48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A finely-woven fabric made originally from linen but often now from cotton."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eebd4cf0-f220-4e17-b4d7-31379ccbaacb",
                                                "sense_id": "23bff8ad-3dee-38ca-afa3-99626b856140",
                                                "text": "Could a Taff'ta ſcarf, a long Eſtridge vvhing, / A ſtiffe Iron Doublet, and a Brazeel Pole / Tempt thee from Cambrick ſheets, fine active Thighs, / From Caudles vvhere the precious Amber ſvvims?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ac48999-ea71-4178-ae0d-e5f0c0fef65d",
                                                "sense_id": "23bff8ad-3dee-38ca-afa3-99626b856140",
                                                "text": "Scotch cambric, now largely manufactured, is a kind of imitation cambric, made from fine hard-twisted cotton."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20624729-bd1a-4c84-b143-c58cc3f252c7",
                                                "sense_id": "23bff8ad-3dee-38ca-afa3-99626b856140",
                                                "text": "His upper tunic was of white cambric, as fine as a handkerchief, so that the bright red tunic beneath it showed through."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "76dc6749-3fce-4fce-83d0-2c915bfd79fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "8b5459df-80f3-3500-8c93-4ea07b160be0",
                        "target_lang_word": "lawn",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25ba12ca-130a-3c6b-9ae2-f576f5169e72",
                                        "entry_id": "5d82aef7-66d2-3971-9af0-1a70b4faa9c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ground (generally in front of or around a house) covered with grass kept closely mown."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8df44417-a078-4471-a59c-8720d29d6b7b",
                                                "sense_id": "25ba12ca-130a-3c6b-9ae2-f576f5169e72",
                                                "text": "Pretty soon I struck into a sort of path[…]. It twisted and turned,[…]and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn. And, back of the lawn, was a big, old-fashioned house, with piazzas stretching in front of it, and all blazing with lights. 'Twas the house I'd seen the roof of from the beach."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "055ab9d1-d740-3ba6-96aa-8b18c1c8088b",
                                        "entry_id": "5d82aef7-66d2-3971-9af0-1a70b4faa9c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An open space between woods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "England",
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "regional",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3baa909-1a6e-3f59-bab1-8c5e2ffc1b95",
                                        "entry_id": "5d82aef7-66d2-3971-9af0-1a70b4faa9c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An overgrown agar culture, such that no separation between single colonies exists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea2d4ff8-ec85-3f9e-b4c6-0f53a36006b7",
                                        "entry_id": "5f65e080-cd2a-3e88-b935-2d170de812c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To furnish with a lawn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a275637-3298-4fec-9226-92f8136cb0f7",
                                                "sense_id": "ea2d4ff8-ec85-3f9e-b4c6-0f53a36006b7",
                                                "text": "By opening all the arches of the several apartments […], by lawning the area within, and by a judicious use of ivy where any blank spaces require to be broken, or any deformities concealed, this might be made a beautiful and singular scene; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "704b5910-3db0-33fe-bc6c-e302d720ca7c",
                                        "entry_id": "3322b890-6b04-3520-977e-789219b1d9f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of thin linen or cotton."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1534213-3ed4-40d4-9f01-4090f31d703f",
                                                "sense_id": "704b5910-3db0-33fe-bc6c-e302d720ca7c",
                                                "text": "Two hundred Sempſtreſſes were employed to make me Shirts, and Linen for Bed and Table, all of the ſtrongeft and coarſeſt kind they could get; which, however, they were forced to quilt together in ſeveral Folds, for the thickeſt was ſome degrees finer than Lawn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e1c62db-5d92-4830-89be-db93c4b1088a",
                                                "sense_id": "704b5910-3db0-33fe-bc6c-e302d720ca7c",
                                                "text": "The stream had trickled over her chin and stained the purity of her lawn death robe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4e86b05-b739-4082-83b6-b03a815d8093",
                                                "sense_id": "704b5910-3db0-33fe-bc6c-e302d720ca7c",
                                                "text": "He looked through the glass at the fire, set it down on the end of the desk and wiped his lips with a sheer lawn handkerchief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecf14950-478a-339f-8e54-c396200d7a14",
                                        "entry_id": "3322b890-6b04-3520-977e-789219b1d9f5",
                                        "glosses": [
